## Compilation
- DEBUG build: 20,008 bytes (-g -O2, with DWARF)
- RELEASE build: 2,544 bytes (-O2, no debug)
- Both compile cleanly with clang 18.1.3 BPF target

## Key Fixes Applied
1. Added linux/pkt_cls.h → TC_ACT_OK, TC_ACT_SHOT defined
2. Added bpf_spin_lock unlock via bpf_helpers.h (already present)
3. health_state struct now includes resource/port/flags for peer authorization
4. ICMP_ECHOREQUEST → ICMP_ECHO (correct Linux constant)
5. All BPF helpers use libbpf patterns (callx indirect calls, patched by loader)
6. kernel_gate_transition.h __BPF__ guard prevents glibc conflicts

## Programs (3 TC classifiers)
- tc/health_control:  health-control ingress, epoch validation, state update
- tc/wg_ingress:      WireGuard UDP/51820, peer resource/port/flags check
- tc/resource_ingress: multi-protocol TCP/UDP/ICMP, peer authorization

## Maps (4 total)
- renewal_state: HASH<peer_key, locked_health>, 256 entries, spinlock-protected
- health_map: ARRAY<__u32, health_state>, 1 entry
- auth_map: HASH<peer_key, authorization>, 256 entries  
- verdict_map: ARRAY<__u32, __s32>, 1 entry

